{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(pattern_array: list[str], sequence_array: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a sequence follows a pattern based on consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Ensures elements re-occur consistently in both pattern and sequence arrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(pattern_array) != len(sequence_array):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_seq_map = {}\n    seq_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(pattern_array)):\n        pattern_element = pattern_array[i]\n        sequence_element = sequence_array[i]\n\n        # Check mapping from pattern to sequence\n        if pattern_element in pattern_to_seq_map:\n            if pattern_to_seq_map[pattern_element] != sequence_element:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_seq_map[pattern_element] = sequence_element\n\n        # Check mapping from sequence to pattern\n        if sequence_element in seq_to_pattern_map:\n            if seq_to_pattern_map[sequence_element] != pattern_element:\n                return False\n        else:\n            seq_to_pattern_map[sequence_element] = pattern_element\n\n    return True"}
