{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    It adheres to the recursive definition P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1)) for n > 2.\"\"\"\n    if not hasattr(sequence, \"_cache\"):\n        sequence._cache = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    if n in sequence._cache:\n        return sequence._cache[n]\n\n    # P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1)) for n > 2\n    p_n_minus_1_value = sequence(n - 1)\n\n    term1 = sequence(p_n_minus_1_value)\n    term2 = sequence(n - p_n_minus_1_value)\n\n    result = term1 + term2\n    sequence._cache[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number's digits alternate, like 121 or 12121. Single-digit numbers are considered undulating.\"\"\"\n    s_num = str(number)\n    n = len(s_num)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        # Adjacent digits must be different.\n        if s_num[i] == s_num[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n        # Digits two positions apart must be the same (e.g., d0=d2, d1=d3).\n        if i + 2 < n:\n            if s_num[i] != s_num[i+2]:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
