{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given positive integer n.\n    A proper divisor is a positive divisor of a number, excluding the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n\n    divisors_sum = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divisors_sum += i\n            if i * i != n:\n                divisors_sum += n // i\n    return divisors_sum\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 up to the specified limit (inclusive).\n    An amicable pair (a, b) consists of two different numbers with specific proper divisor sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for a in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if a in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        b_candidate = sum_proper_divisors(a)\n\n        if a != b_candidate and b_candidate <= limit:\n            a_candidate = sum_proper_divisors(b_candidate)\n            if a == a_candidate:\n                total_sum += a + b_candidate\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(a)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(b_candidate)\n\n    return total_sum"}
