{"task_id": "Mbpp/124", "solution": "import cmath\ndef angle_complex(real_component, imaginary_component):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the angle (argument) of a complex number in radians.\n    Constructs the complex number by directly adding components, then uses cmath.phase.\"\"\"\n\n    # Construct the complex number by directly adding real_component and imaginary_component.\n    # Python's built-in arithmetic handles different numeric types correctly.\n    z = real_component + imaginary_component\n\n    # Calculate the angle (phase) of the complex number using cmath.phase().\n    angle_in_radians = cmath.phase(z)\n\n    return angle_in_radians"}
