{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(array: list, n: int, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of the given element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    first_idx = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_idx\ndef _find_last_occurrence(array: list, n: int, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the last occurrence of the given element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    last_idx = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_idx = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_idx\ndef is_majority(array: list, n: int, element: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > (n / 2)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(array: list, n: int, x: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of x in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    first_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == x:\n            first_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_index\ndef _find_last_occurrence(array: list, n: int, x: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the last occurrence of x in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    last_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == x:\n            last_index = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_index\ndef is_majority(array: list, n: int, x: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given element x is a 'majority element' in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, n, x)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, n, x)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > (n / 2)"}
