{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of sequences of length n, where each element is\n    at least twice the previous and at most m.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[length][start_value] stores the count of valid sequences\n    # of 'length' starting with 'start_value'.\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: For sequences of length 1, any value from 1 to m is valid.\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 up to n.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for current_val in range(1, m + 1):\n            # The next element in the sequence must be at least twice the current_val\n            # and must not exceed m.\n            for next_val in range(2 * current_val, m + 1):\n                dp[length][current_val] += dp[length - 1][next_val]\n\n    # The total count is the sum of all valid sequences of length n,\n    # starting with any possible value from 1 to m.\n    total_count = sum(dp[n][i] for i in range(1, m + 1))\n    return total_count"}
