{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "from typing import Union\nimport math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    Handles non-positive inputs according to specification (e.g., 0 for negative, 1 for 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    root = math.sqrt(number)\n\n    if root == int(root):\n        next_root = int(root) + 1\n    else:\n        next_root = math.ceil(root)\n\n    return next_root * next_root"}
