{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "import math\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is prime.\n    It efficiently checks for divisibility up to its integer square root.\"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    limit = math.isqrt(num)\n    for i in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\ndef count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than a given non-negative integer n.\n    It iterates from 2 to n-1 and uses a helper function to determine primality.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n\n    return prime_count"}
