{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def _sieve_of_eratosthenes(limit: int) -> list[bool]:\n    \"\"\"Helper function to find primes up to 'limit-1' using Sieve of Eratosthenes.\n    Returns a boolean list where `is_prime[i]` is True if `i` is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if limit <= 2:\n        return [False] * limit\n\n    is_prime = [True] * limit\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n\n    for p in range(2, int(limit**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            for multiple in range(p * p, limit, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n    return is_prime\ndef count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes to efficiently find primes.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    is_prime_flags = _sieve_of_eratosthenes(number)\n    prime_count = sum(is_prime_flags[2:])\n    return prime_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "def combinations_colors(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"Generates all combinations with repetition from input_list for a given length n.\n    Returns a list of tuples, where each tuple is a combination.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n\n    # Inner recursive function to build combinations.\n    def _recursive_combinations(current_combo_elements, length_remaining):\n        # Base case: if no more elements are needed, a combination is complete.\n        if length_remaining == 0:\n            results.append(tuple(current_combo_elements))\n            return\n\n        # Recursive step: for each item in the input list, extend the current combo and recurse.\n        for item in input_list:\n            _recursive_combinations(current_combo_elements + [item], length_remaining - 1)\n\n    _recursive_combinations([], n)\n    return results"}
