{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "import math\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], length: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum contiguous subarray sum in an array repeated k times.\n    Utilizes Kadane's algorithm for subarray sum calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_max_subarray_sum(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Applies Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray.\n        Handles arrays with all negative numbers correctly.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not nums:\n            return 0  # Should not happen given problem constraints, but robust.\n\n        max_so_far = nums[0]\n        current_max = nums[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n            current_max = max(nums[i], current_max + nums[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return _calculate_max_subarray_sum(arr)\n\n    # For k > 1, consider cases where the max subarray spans across original array boundaries.\n    # Calculate max sum for a doubled array (arr + arr).\n    doubled_arr = arr + arr\n    max_sum_double_pass = _calculate_max_subarray_sum(doubled_arr)\n\n    # Calculate the total sum of the original array.\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # If the total sum is positive, additional repetitions of the array will contribute positively.\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        # The total sum could be extended by (k - 2) full repetitions of the array.\n        max_sum_spanning = max_sum_double_pass + (k - 2) * total_sum\n        return max(max_sum_double_pass, max_sum_spanning)\n    else:\n        # If total_sum is non-positive, further repetitions won't increase the sum.\n        return max_sum_double_pass"}
