{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "def dict_depth(dictionary):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum depth of nested dictionaries.\n    Depth is 1 for a dictionary with no nested dictionaries.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_current_depth = 0\n    for value in dictionary.values():\n        try:\n            # Attempt to recurse on the value. If the value is not a dictionary\n            # (or dict-like), the recursive call will raise an AttributeError\n            # or TypeError when it tries to access .values() on a non-dict type.\n            current_sub_depth = dict_depth(value)\n            max_current_depth = max(max_current_depth, current_sub_depth)\n        except (AttributeError, TypeError):\n            # Catch errors that occur if 'value' is not a dictionary and thus\n            # cannot be processed by dict_depth; effectively ignoring non-dictionary values.\n            pass\n    return 1 + max_current_depth"}
