{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(input_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of elements within each tuple and returns the minimum product.\n    This function assumes input_list is non-empty and contains valid tuples.\"\"\"\n\n    # Initialize the minimum product with the product of the first tuple.\n    # Per design, assume input_list is valid and non-empty.\n    min_prod = input_list[0][0] * input_list[0][1]\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the list to find the overall minimum product.\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        current_tuple = input_list[i]\n        current_prod = current_tuple[0] * current_tuple[1]\n        if current_prod < min_prod:\n            min_prod = current_prod\n\n    return min_prod"}
