{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(input_array: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the pair of integers from an input array that yields the highest product.\n    It considers products of the two largest numbers and the two smallest numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max1 = float('-inf')  # Stores the largest number found.\n    max2 = float('-inf')  # Stores the second largest number found.\n    min1 = float('inf')   # Stores the smallest number found.\n    min2 = float('inf')   # Stores the second smallest number found.\n\n    for num in input_array:\n        # Update largest and second largest numbers.\n        if num > max1:\n            max2 = max1\n            max1 = num\n        elif num > max2:\n            max2 = num\n\n        # Update smallest and second smallest numbers.\n        if num < min1:\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = num\n        elif num < min2:\n            min2 = num\n\n    # Calculate products from the two largest and two smallest numbers.\n    product_of_two_largest = max1 * max2\n    product_of_two_smallest = min1 * min2\n\n    # Return the pair with the highest product, in ascending order.\n    if product_of_two_largest >= product_of_two_smallest:\n        return (min(max1, max2), max(max1, max2))\n    else:\n        return (min(min1, min2), max(min1, min2))"}
