{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(input_array: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list containing the sorted numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = input_array.copy()\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Initialize gap, then reduce it in each pass.\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Perform gapped insertion sort for current gap size.\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "def median_trapezium(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium.\n\n    The median length of a trapezium is the average of its two parallel sides.\n    Based on the assert statement, the first two arguments (a and b) are\n    considered the lengths of the parallel sides. The third argument (c)\n    is extraneous for this calculation.\n\n    Args:\n        a (float or int): The length of the first parallel side.\n        b (float or int): The length of the second parallel side.\n        c (float or int): An extraneous argument, not used in the calculation\n                          of the median length of a trapezium.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The median length of the trapezium.\n    \"\"\"\n    return (a + b) / 2"}
