{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "_perrin_cache = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 2}\ndef _get_perrin_number(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the k-th Perrin number using memoization.\n    It retrieves from cache or computes recursively, storing the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k not in _perrin_cache:\n        # Calculate P(k) using the recurrence relation and store it.\n        _perrin_cache[k] = _get_perrin_number(k - 2) + _get_perrin_number(k - 3)\n    return _perrin_cache[k]\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    It uses a memoized helper function to efficiently compute Perrin numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle base cases for n=0, 1, 2 directly from the cache.\n    if n == 0:\n        return _perrin_cache[0]\n    elif n == 1:\n        return _perrin_cache[0] + _perrin_cache[1]\n    elif n == 2:\n        return _perrin_cache[0] + _perrin_cache[1] + _perrin_cache[2]\n    else: # For n > 2, sum initial values and iterate.\n        current_sum = _perrin_cache[0] + _perrin_cache[1] + _perrin_cache[2]\n        # Iterate from P(3) up to P(n), adding each to the sum.\n        for k in range(3, n + 1):\n            current_sum += _get_perrin_number(k)\n        return current_sum"}
