{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[float | int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within a given array.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero numbers by tracking max and min products ending at the current position.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = float(arr[0])\n    min_so_far = float(arr[0])\n    result = float(arr[0])\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = float(arr[i])\n\n        # If the current number is negative, multiplying it will reverse the roles\n        # of max_so_far and min_so_far for the next calculations.\n        if num < 0:\n            max_so_far, min_so_far = min_so_far, max_so_far\n\n        # Update max_so_far to be the maximum of the current number itself\n        # or the product of max_so_far (potentially swapped) and the current number.\n        max_so_far = max(num, max_so_far * num)\n\n        # Update min_so_far to be the minimum of the current number itself\n        # or the product of min_so_far (potentially swapped) and the current number.\n        min_so_far = min(num, min_so_far * num)\n\n        # The overall result is the maximum seen so far, including the current max_so_far.\n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n    return int(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef max_subarray_product(arr: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of any contiguous subarray within the input array.\n    It tracks the max and min products ending at the current position to handle negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = arr[0]\n    current_min = arr[0]\n    global_max = arr[0]\n\n    for num in arr[1:]:\n        # Store current_max before it's updated, as it's needed for current_min calculation.\n        temp_current_max = current_max\n\n        # Update current_max: it can be num, or num * previous max, or num * previous min.\n        current_max = max(num, num * temp_current_max, num * current_min)\n        # Update current_min: it can be num, or num * previous max, or num * previous min.\n        current_min = min(num, num * temp_current_max, num * current_min)\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n\n    return global_max"}
