{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of numbers in a list whose bitwise XOR sum is odd.\n    An XOR sum is odd if one number is odd and the other is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    even_count = 0\n\n    for num in arr:\n        if num % 2 != 0:  # Check if the number is odd\n            odd_count += 1\n        else:  # The number is even\n            even_count += 1\n\n    # The total number of pairs with an odd XOR sum is (odd_count * even_count)\n    return odd_count * even_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def _is_odd_xor_sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the bitwise XOR sum of two numbers is odd.\n    Returns True if odd, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return (num1 ^ num2) % 2 != 0\ndef find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR sum is odd.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs and uses a helper to check parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_pair_count = 0\n    for i in range(length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            if _is_odd_xor_sum(input_list[i], input_list[j]):\n                odd_pair_count += 1\n    return odd_pair_count"}
