{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "def catalan_number(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Catalan number using an iterative formula. Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    catalan = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        catalan = catalan * (2 * (2 * i + 1)) // (i + 2)\n    return catalan"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "import math\ndef surface_Area(base_edge: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total surface area of a square pyramid.\n    Trusts that inputs are positive numerical values as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR3: Compute the base area\n    base_area = base_edge * base_edge\n\n    # FR4: Compute the slant height using the specified formula\n    # Critical requirement #2 prevents custom MathUtils, so math.sqrt is used.\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(height**2 + (base_edge/2)**2)\n\n    # FR5: Compute the lateral surface area\n    lateral_surface_area = 2 * base_edge * slant_height\n\n    # FR6: Sum the base area and the lateral surface area to determine the total\n    total_surface_area = base_area + lateral_surface_area\n\n    # FR7: Return the calculated total surface area\n    return total_surface_area"}
