{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(num1: int, num2: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a list of perfect squares within an inclusive numerical range.\n    The range is defined by num1 and num2.\n    \"\"\"\n    actual_min = min(num1, num2)\n    actual_max = max(num1, num2)\n\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n\n    # Calculate the smallest integer whose square is within or just above actual_min.\n    # Per design, trust inputs such that actual_min >= 0 for sqrt.\n    start_sqrt_val = math.ceil(math.sqrt(actual_min))\n\n    # Calculate the largest integer whose square is within or just below actual_max.\n    end_sqrt_val = math.floor(math.sqrt(actual_max))\n\n    for i in range(int(start_sqrt_val), int(end_sqrt_val) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        perfect_squares_list.append(square)\n\n    return perfect_squares_list"}
