{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "from typing import List, Optional\ndef is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is even.\n    Returns True if the number is even, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\ndef is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is odd.\n    Returns True if the number is odd, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\ndef find_first_even(numbers: List[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first even number in a list.\n    Returns the first even number found, or None if no even number is present.\"\"\"\n    for number in numbers:\n        if is_even(number):\n            return number\n    return None\ndef find_first_odd(numbers: List[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first odd number in a list.\n    Returns the first odd number found, or None if no odd number is present.\"\"\"\n    for number in numbers:\n        if is_odd(number):\n            return number\n    return None\ndef calculate_absolute_difference(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the absolute difference between two integers.\n    Returns the non-negative difference.\"\"\"\n    return abs(num1 - num2)\ndef diff_even_odd(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates finding the first even and first odd numbers and calculating their absolute difference.\n    It trusts that the input list will contain both an even and an odd number.\"\"\"\n    first_even = find_first_even(numbers)\n    first_odd = find_first_odd(numbers)\n    # Per critical requirements, assume inputs are valid and no None checks or error raising needed here.\n    return calculate_absolute_difference(first_even, first_odd)"}
