{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle given its radius.\n    Returns None if the radius is negative as per FR4.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n\n    # The largest triangle has a base equal to the diameter (2*radius).\n    # Its height is equal to the radius of the semicircle.\n    base = 2 * radius\n    height = radius\n\n    area = 0.5 * base * height\n\n    return area"}
