{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from top-left to bottom-right in a matrix.\n    Paths are restricted to moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Base case: The cost to reach (0,0) is its own value.\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill the first row: Only possible to come from the left.\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1] + matrix[0][j]\n\n    # Fill the first column: Only possible to come from above.\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i-1][0] + matrix[i][0]\n\n    # Fill the remaining DP table: Choose the path (from above or left) that yields the maximum sum.\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(1, N):\n            dp[i][j] = matrix[i][j] + max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The total number of cells in any path from (0,0) to (N-1, N-1) in an N*N grid is fixed.\n    num_cells = 2 * N - 1\n\n    # The maximum average is the maximum total sum divided by the fixed number of cells.\n    return float(dp[N-1][N-1]) / num_cells"}
