{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "import math\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index k of the smallest triangular number T_k that has exactly n digits.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer representing the desired number of digits.\n\n    Returns:\n        A positive integer k, the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # The smallest n-digit number is 10^(n-1).\n    # We are looking for the smallest k such that T_k = k * (k + 1) / 2 >= 10^(n-1).\n    # This leads to the inequality k^2 + k - 2 * 10^(n-1) >= 0.\n    # We can find the positive root of the quadratic equation k^2 + k - 2 * 10^(n-1) = 0.\n    # k = (-1 + sqrt(1 - 4 * 1 * (-2 * 10^(n-1)))) / 2\n    # k = (-1 + sqrt(1 + 8 * 10^(n-1))) / 2\n    # We use math.ceil to get the smallest integer k that satisfies the inequality.\n    k = math.ceil((-1 + math.sqrt(1 + 8 * (10**(n - 1)))) / 2)\n\n    return int(k)"}
