{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "def find_min_diff(arr: tuple[int, ...], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the input tuple.\n    Returns `int(float('inf'))` if `n < 2`.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        # Handles cases with fewer than two elements as per design.\n        return int(float('inf'))\n\n    # Sorts the input tuple to simplify finding minimum differences.\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n\n    # Initializes minimum difference with a large value.\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterates through the sorted array to find the smallest adjacent difference.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        current_diff = abs(sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i])\n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = current_diff\n\n    return int(min_diff)"}
