{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "def count_divisors(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer has an even number of positive divisors.\n    Returns True if the divisor count is even, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisor_count = 0\n    # Iterate up to the square root of n to find divisors efficiently.\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i * i == n:\n                # If i is the square root, it's a single divisor.\n                divisor_count += 1\n            else:\n                # Otherwise, i and n/i are two distinct divisors.\n                divisor_count += 2\n        i += 1\n\n    # Return True if the total number of divisors is even, False otherwise.\n    return divisor_count % 2 == 0"}
