{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def find_last_position(arr: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    last_occurrence_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            last_occurrence_index = mid  # Store this as a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1              # Continue searching in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return last_occurrence_index"}
