{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer.\n    The rotation amount `d` is normalized to be within [0, 31].\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_SIZE = 32\n    mask = 0xFFFFFFFF  # 32-bit mask\n\n    # Normalize rotation amount\n    d = d % BIT_SIZE\n\n    # Perform left shift and mask to keep within 32 bits\n    shifted_left_part = (number << d) & mask\n\n    # Perform right shift to get the bits that wrap around\n    wrapped_around_part = (number >> (BIT_SIZE - d))\n\n    # Combine the two parts\n    return shifted_left_part | wrapped_around_part"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a 32-bit integer's bits left by d positions, handling wrap-around.\n    The input `number` is treated as a 32-bit unsigned integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Mask number to 32 bits and normalize shift amount.\n    num_32bit = number & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    shift_amount = d % 32\n\n    # Perform the rotation and mask the result to ensure it stays within 32 bits.\n    return ((num_32bit << shift_amount) | (num_32bit >> (32 - shift_amount))) & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
